WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.362
The federal requirement, from
the guide's requirements table.

2
00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:09.123
Gate nine supports I R four, enhancement
one, automated incident handling processes,

3
00:00:09.123 --> 00:00:14.061
and S I four, enhancement seven,
automated response to suspicious events,

4
00:00:14.061 --> 00:00:18.999
from NIST special publication eight
hundred fifty-three, revision five.

5
00:00:18.999 --> 00:00:21.599
The evidence is the device group levels,

6
00:00:21.599 --> 00:00:24.513
the exclusions, and the
Action center export.

7
00:00:24.513 --> 00:00:28.996
Gate ten supports C A seven,
continuous monitoring; A U eleven,

8
00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:33.750
audit record retention; and I R
three, incident response testing.

9
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.525
The evidence is the monthly
package and the exercise record.

10
00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:41.631
Each row lines up with fed-ramp
twenty X key security indicators,

11
00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:46.900
which bind cloud service providers; the
agency lines its own evidence up with them.

12
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:51.525
The guide counts Gates two, seven
and ten, with the synthetic events,

13
00:00:51.525 --> 00:00:54.637
as the closure map's
audit and visibility row.

14
00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:56.728
The gates support these controls,

15
00:00:56.728 --> 00:01:00.000
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.
